	Is it my imagination, or are there no drow elves in Nethack? It
shouldn't be hard.

	My last original idea: a ring of swimming.  Confers the intrinsic "You
can swim."  A scroll should be available that can do the same.  You can't get
a kraken corpse, but maybe a tin of kraken meat (if it exists) could also
grant the intrinsic.

	My 2 cents on the Terminator idea: I was watching T2 last month when
I came up with this idea independently.  Only I thought the T-1000 should be a
breed of `m' with the powers of giant mimics and chameleons (not affected by
cancellation, but protection from shape changers should have some interesting
effect).  ~200 HP was my concept.  I had considered the wand-of-cold/scroll of
fire concept, but thought that was too closed-ended.  As for the "out of
context" argument, I maintain that anachronism and mixed metaphor are the very
soul of Nethack.  Otherwise, why have Archaeologists and Cavemen in the same
dungeon? Or Elves and long worms? etc.  T-1000 doesn't have to be a high tech
idea, and no extraneous plot line need be spun.

